@startuml j9-shared-tickets
!include style.iuml
title J9 Tickets shared across devices (v1.3)
actor Patient
participant "Chat page\n(index.html, chat.js, sync.js)" as Chat
participant "core.js" as Core
database "localStorage\n(patient's phone)" as LS
participant "Ticket function\n(/api/tickets)" as Fn
database "Ticket store\n(server, seven days)" as Store
participant "Staff page on another device\n(staff/index.html, staff.js, sync.js)" as SP
actor Staff
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : asks a question on a phone
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(q, data)
Core --> Chat : the reply from the clinic file, as always
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket({...})
Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets (the ticket stays in the phone's browser)
Chat --> Patient : the answer
Chat -> LS : read frontdesk.synckey (made once, this browser's private key)
Chat -> Fn : sync.js sends the ticket with the browser's private key
alt the store is set up and the call gets through
  Fn -> Fn : cleans the ticket, makes a hash of the key
  Fn -> Store : one record for the ticket with owner = the hash;\nits id added to the ordered list and to the owner's set
  note right of Fn
  v1.3. The question, reply and patient
  never change once stored. The record
  is kept for seven days.
  end note
  Fn --> Chat : stored
  Chat --> Patient : the small print now says the messages go to the clinic's front desk
else no store configured, or the call is blocked
  Fn --> Chat : no store (or no answer)
  Chat --> Patient : the chat works as before; the add-on goes quiet
end

Staff -> SP : open /staff on another device
SP --> Staff : their own tickets only
Staff -> SP : turn on "Show tickets from all devices"
SP -> SP : write frontdesk.alldevices; ask for the clinic's desk code
Staff -> SP : type the desk code (sessionStorage frontdesk.deskcode, this session only)
SP -> Fn : sync.js asks for the list with the desk code
alt no desk code set on the server
  Fn --> SP : 403, no list
  SP --> Staff : "the clinic has not set one on the server yet"
else no desk code typed, or a wrong one
  Fn --> SP : 401, no list; the page asks for the code
  SP --> Staff : their own tickets only, as before
else the desk code matches the one in the server's environment
  Fn -> Store : read the ordered list and its records (staff ask about every 5 s)
  Fn --> SP : the list of tickets
  SP --> Staff : the patient's ticket appears, marked as from another device (remote)
  Staff -> SP : types in #staff-reply, presses #staff-send
  SP -> Core : FD.replyToTicket(id, text)
  SP -> Fn : sync.js sends the change with the desk code
  Fn -> Store : merge: every staff reply kept, the status further along wins
  loop every 10 s for ten minutes after the last change, then once a minute up to half an hour
    Chat -> Fn : sync.js fetches this browser's own tickets with its private key
    Fn -> Store : read the owner's set of ids and their records
    Fn --> Chat : the tickets of this owner only
  end
  Chat -> Core : merge the staff reply into the ticket
  Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets
  Chat --> Patient : .bot-msg marked "From the clinic team"
  note over Chat, SP : the ticket is answered on both devices
end

opt A stranger holds a ticket id and a patient id, but another key
  Fn <-] : read or change that ticket
  Fn -> Fn : the hash of the key is not the ticket's owner
  Fn -->] : 403, nothing readable, nothing changed
end
note over Chat, SP : without a store both pages work as in 1.2; a patient reads with the browser's key, staff with the desk code; the staff reply path is J4
@enduml
